lict on P-CONFLICT-3. That gives 12 cells below 0.6 and production mismatches on P-BOUNDARY-1 and P-CONFLICT-3. All three new bundles are exact. B3 ranks first: 66/66 cells, 22/22 verdicts, 11/11 stable, zero regressions, 66/66 cells >= 0.8, minimum 0.98, and no production mismatch. The m-3 diagnostic is satisfied 4/4 at >= 0.98 (B0 on the same item: relevance 0.64-1.0, live fix1 0.49-0.61); the tune did not aim at it.", "gate": "planning", "operation": "tune", "oracle_sha256": "b3cd6d7907d3e0f8aa9fb8d3b8d5efafbde5f34574648ba742528a7ef19dc199", "planner_action": "lint-m-3 needs no ANC-012 edit. After review, add the ANC-012 entry to overrides-plan.json from the sealed question set (proposed file overrides-plan.proposed.json), store tuning_history_after, then re-run check-fixtures and the planning gate at 0.6. Note: ANC-012 is a prohibition, so the gate ignores the addressed role; it is tuned for exactness only.", "production_confidence_threshold": 0.6, "production_semantics_unchanged": true, "question_action": null, "sealed_question_set": {"digest": "5bece6f6b17e5acfdde8b5c45782ff59b5628dbacfaaf1181ca140336e22c882", "questions": {"addressed": {"criteria": {"no": "No such commitment is written, or the item adds a setup, hook or interpreter key.", "unclear": "A sentence touches this but cannot be read as the commitment or not.", "yes": "Such a commitment is written in the item."}, "instructions": "Is there a sentence in `item.text` committing that sc-lint.toml gains no setup-hook key and no interpreter-selection key (for example setup or runner stay unknown keys)? Plans that add such a key contain no such commitment. Judge only whether the commitment is written.", "type": "choice"}, "contradicted": {"criteria": {"no": "The item plans no such key.", "unclear": "The item plans a key whose role cannot be told.", "yes": "The item plans a setup-hook or interpreter-selection key."}, "instructions": "Conflict means the item adds or keeps a sc-lint.toml key that runs setup or